    ("What is printed?\nint x = 10, *p = &x, *q = p;\n*q = 20;\nprintf(\"%d\", x);", ["20", "10", "An address", "30"], 0, "p and q both point to x."),
    ("What is printed?\nchar s[] = \"KEA\", *p = s + 1;\nprintf(\"%s\", p);", ["EA", "KEA", "E", "A"], 0, "p points to the second character."),
    ("What is printed?\nchar *p = \"Bengaluru\";\nprintf(\"%c\", p[3]);", ["g", "n", "a", "e"], 0, "B(0) e(1) n(2) g(3)."),
    ("What is printed?\nint a[3] = {5, 10, 15}, *p = &a[2];\nprintf(\"%d\", *p - *(p - 2));", ["10", "5", "15", "2"], 0, "15 − 5."),
    ("What is printed?\nint a[] = {2, 4, 6}, *p = a;\np++;\nprintf(\"%d\", ++*p);", ["5", "4", "6", "3"], 0, "++*p increments a[1] from 4 to 5."),
    ("What is printed?\nint a[] = {2, 4, 6}, *p = a;\nprintf(\"%d\", *++p);", ["4", "2", "3", "6"], 0, "*++p moves p first, then dereferences."),
    ("What is printed?\nint a[10], *p = &a[7], *q = &a[2];\nprintf(\"%d\", (int)(p - q));", ["5", "20", "7", "2"], 0, P + "The difference counts elements, not bytes."),
    ("For  int a[10], *p = &a[7], *q = &a[2];  the value of  p > q  is", ["1", "0", "5", "Undefined"], 0, "Pointers into the same array can be compared."),
