    ("What is printed?\nstruct st { char n; int m; } s[2] = {{'A', 50}, {'B', 70}};\nstruct st *p = s;\np++;\nprintf(\"%c\", p->n);", ["B", "A", "An address", "Garbage"], 0,
     "p + 1 moves to the next structure."),
    ("With 8-byte aligned double, sizeof(struct { char a; double b; }) is", ["16", "9", "8", "12"], 0, P + "7 padding bytes after a."),
    ("With 2-byte short, sizeof(struct { char a; char b; short c; }) is", ["4", "6", "3", "8"], 0, "No padding is needed."),
    ("sizeof(struct { int a[3]; char c; }) with 4-byte int is", ["16", "13", "12", "15"], 0, "12 + 1, padded to a multiple of 4."),
    ("What is printed?\nstruct pt { int x, y; };\nvoid f(struct pt t) { t.x = 0; }\n…\nstruct pt a = {1, 2};\nf(a);\nprintf(\"%d\", a.x);", ["1", "0", "2", "Garbage"], 0,
     "f works on a copy."),
    ("What is printed?\nstruct pt { int x, y; };\nvoid g(struct pt *t) { t->x = 0; }\n…\nstruct pt a = {1, 2};\ng(&a);\nprintf(\"%d\", a.x);", ["0", "1", "2", "Garbage"], 0,
     "g works through a pointer."),
    ("union { int i; float f; } u;  u.f = 1.0f;  printf(\"%d\", u.i);  prints", ["1065353216 – the bit pattern of 1.0f read as an int", "1", "0", "1.000000"], 0,
     P + "1.0f is 0x3F800000."),
    ("sizeof(union { char c[7]; int i; }) with 4-byte int is", ["8", "7", "11", "4"], 0, "7 rounded up to a multiple of 4."),
    ("After  typedef struct node *NodePtr;  the declaration  NodePtr p;  declares p as", ["A pointer to struct node", "A struct node", "An int", "An error"], 0,
     "Common in linked-list code."),
    ("What is printed?\nenum { A, B, C } x = B;\nprintf(\"%d\", x + C);", ["3", "2", "1", "BC"], 0, "B = 1, C = 2."),
    ("enum { X = -2, Y, Z };  — the value of Z is", ["0", "1", "−1", "2"], 0, "−2, −1, 0."),
    ("struct { unsigned a : 4, b : 4; } s;  typically has sizeof(s) equal to", ["4", "1", "8", "2"], 0, "Both fields fit in one unsigned int (implementation-defined)."),
    ("signed int x : 3;  (a bit field) can hold", ["−4 to 3", "0 to 7", "−3 to 3", "−8 to 7"], 0, P + "3-bit two's complement."),
