    ("What is printed?\nstruct n { int d; struct n *nx; } c = {3, NULL}, b = {2, &c}, a = {1, &b};\nstruct n *p;\nint s = 0;\nfor (p = &a; p; p = p->nx) s += p->d;\nprintf(\"%d\", s);",
     ["6", "1", "3", "An infinite loop"], 0, "Traversing a three-node linked list."),
